From 63440de62e60cd8e0432027a36efbf9305a4f2f7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: JimmyBlunt <jo@paso-music.de>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 21:23:11 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 09/12] FastLED example catalogue and multi-file FastLED
 Patterns (local #9002)

Catalogue (all 114 official FastLED examples, FastLED 3.10.5 @ ec0a0f35):
- Vendored read-only in src/engine/fastled/catalog/ (fastled-examples.json
  schema 1 + verbatim compile files, sha256-checked; .gitattributes -text so
  bytes stay exact). scripts/sync-fastled-catalog.mjs re-imports from the
  engine's catalog/ folder. Index and every file load lazily
  (fastledCatalogLoader.ts, import.meta.glob ?raw): no main-bundle growth.
- Patterns rail: "FastLED" built-in folder with catalogue categories,
  collapsed like the stock sections; hardware examples marked "HW" with
  their German note as tooltip.
- An example opens read-only under the built-in key fastled:<id> (the
  activeDemoName slot of stock demos): header (marker, @pxlblz-dim,
  @pxlblz-main, provenance, hardware note) + verbatim sketch + supporting
  files. Banner with the note; recommended pixel count = example LED count;
  compile diagnostics also reach read-only examples (activePushKey).
- Clone uses the stock demo flow and copies the exact source (title name).
- Routes/last-active/remembered place accept fastled:<id>.

Multi-file FastLED Patterns (no schema change, no migration):
- Supporting files ride in src as whole-line `// @pxlblz-file <path>`
  sections (fastledFiles.ts, exact round trip, path rules = compile
  service: subfolders, .h/.cpp/.ino/.json...). Compile client sends
  {source, files, options.fileName}; diagnostics keep their file.
- Editor: file tabs inside FastLED Patterns only (add/rename/remove,
  per-file error counts), one Monaco model per file, markers per file.

Pre-commit hook checks run manually (hook cannot spawn npx.cmd on Windows/Node 24):
eslint on all changed src files, check:e2e-coverage, check:e2e-locators,
tsc (full -b OOMs on this low-memory PC; focused tsc -p over all changed
files/tests incl. App/Editor/PatternList: clean), vitest fastledFiles,
fastledCompileClient, fastledCatalog, fastledStore, Editor.fastled,
PatternList -t built-in, App -t "FastLED catalogue example" (all passed).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
